 ruled out. First, diff_snapshots reports Jaccard 0.0 in both the 38052/43052 and 28052/53052 comparisons, but inspection of the node ids shows only the emitting group member changes (556/658 -> 674/876), while the destination contacts are the same; the edge-level metric is blind to this. Second, the peak_change of 1.0 at t~41834 sits inside an activity hole of a single event in 42052-44051, which collapsed the post-set to one node and forced zero overlap; the change curve rises and decays symmetrically around the gap and returns to baseline, unlike a genuine switch which stays elevated. The underlying mechanism is round-robin rotation of duty among the twelve members over a fixed audience: all members show near-identical totals (90-95 events, 30-35 partners) over the full window while being active in staggered, largely non-overlapping bins."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**The candidate signal turned out to be two artifacts, not a regime switch.**\n\n**1. The \"Jaccard = 0.0\" diffs are an artifact of edge labeling.** Both step_03 (38052\u201343051 vs 43052\u201348052) and step_07 (28052\u201333052 vs 53052\u201358052) report complete edge turnover. But reading the actual node ids: `556\u2192150, 556\u2192204, 556\u2192262...` is *removed* while `674\u2192150, 674\u2192204, 674\u2192262...` is *added*. The **contact set is identical**; only which group member emits the edges changed. Directly confirmed: node 327 in the early window (step_09), node 876 in the middle window (step_13), and node 1676 in the late window (step_10) each contact the **exact same 30 nodes**: {150, 204, 207, 224, 230, 262, 487, 640, 788, 823, 913, 916, 992, 1010, 1132, 1165, 1186, 1294, 1308, 1347, 1372, 1520, 1556, 1575, 1590, 1698, 1728, 1798, 1805, 1938}.\n\n**2. The `peak_change = 1.0` at t\u224841834 (step_04) is a low-data artifact.** It coincides with an activity hole: step_02 shows bin 42052\u201344051 has just **1 event** (vs ~60\u201397 elsewhere), and step_11 confirms only 1 event in 42500\u201343500. With one event on the \"after\" side, the post-set collapsed to the single node {1700}, forcing Jaccard overlap to zero mechanically. The change curve rises and falls smoothly and symmetrically around the gap (0.03\u21921.0\u21920.06), which is the signature of a data hole, not a switch \u2014 a true switch leaves the change level *elevated afterward*.\n\n**3. At the proper 5000-unit half-window, turnover is low and flat.** Step_01 peaks at only **0.268**, and the before/after sets share ~31 of ~37 contacts, differing only in one-off peripherals (358, 585, 1145, 1705 out; 93, 186, 305, 652, 681, 730 in). Step_14 re-centered on 33052\u201353052 peaks at just 0.25. No step change \u2014 the series drifts within 0.12\u20130.27 for the entire period.\n\n**4. The real structure is member rotation on a fixed contact set.** Step_05/step_06 show 556+658 active in 38052\u201343051 (0 events for 674/876), then 674+876 active in 43052\u201348052 (0 events for 556/658). Step_08 shows all twelve members have near-identical totals over the full window (90\u201395 events, 30\u201335 partners) \u2014 each takes a turn. Step_12's low pairwise co-activity (mostly \u22640.4) confirms members are staggered rather than simultaneous.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_d9748f02\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [327, 390, 411, 464, 556, 658, 674, 876, 1220, 1418, 1676, 1838],\n  \"window\": [28052, 58052],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"